\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, O Thou all- victorious Lord,
\par Thy power to us make known;
\par Strike with the hammer of Thy word,
\par And break these hearts of stone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O that we all might now begin
\par Our foolishness to mourn,
\par And turn at once from every sin,
\par And to our Saviour turn!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Give us ourselves and Thee to know,
\par In this our gracious day;
\par Repentance unto life bestow,
\par And take our sins away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Conclude us first in unbelief,
\par And freely then release;
\par Fill every soul with sacred grief,
\par And then with sacred peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Impoverish, Lord, and then relieve,
\par And then enrich the poor;
\par The knowledge of our sickness give;
\par The knowledge of our cure.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. That blessed sense of guilt impart,
\par And then remove the load;
\par Trouble, and wash the troubled heart
\par In the atoning blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Our desperate state through sin declare,
\par And speak our sins forgiven;
\par By perfect holiness prepare,
\par And take us up to heaven.
\par                       Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

